# Generated build output. build.sh recreates all of this; none of it belongs in
# git, and out/ alone reached 53 GB on the build server.
out/
recovery/
rootfs/
buildroot-*/
busybox-*/
*.img
*.img.gz
*.qcow2
*.raw
*.tar.zst
*.sha256

# Upstream sources the build downloads for itself.
payload/dpdk-src.tar.xz
buildroot-*.tar.xz

# The harvested FFN payload. This is the one that must NOT be tracked, and not
# only for size: build.sh tars /opt/ffn-ngfw-v2 off whichever live box it runs
# on, which is how a build host's own configuration ends up inside an appliance
# image. The FFN software is published in FFN-NGFW (its opt/ directory), so a
# build from a clean clone should assemble the payload from repo content instead
# of harvesting a machine. Until it does, this file is a local build input only.
payload/opt-ffn-ngfw-v2.tgz
payload/opt-ffn-ngfw-v1.tgz

# Buildroot output. Regenerate with dprootfs/ffn_octeon_defconfig; keeping an
# 18 MB squashfs in git would freeze a build artifact as if it were source.
dprootfs/*.squashfs

# Timestamped safety copies made while editing on a live box.
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.pre-*
*.orig
*.rej
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Compiled MIPS64 outputs whose source sits beside them (dpagent/*.c).
dpagent/ffn_dpagent
dpagent/ffn_dpagent2
